  "Number": 22,
  "Question": "The logarithm of \\(27\\sqrt[4]{9}\\sqrt[3]{9}\\) to the base \\(3\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\dfrac12\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\dfrac16\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The base-3 logarithm asks which exponent of \\(3\\) produces the given number. Write each positive factor as a power of \\(3\\):\n\\[\n27=3^3,\\qquad\n\\sqrt[4]{9}=3^{2/4}=3^{1/2},\\qquad\n\\sqrt[3]{9}=3^{2/3}.\n\\]\nMultiplying powers with the same positive base adds their exponents, so\n\\[\n27\\sqrt[4]{9}\\sqrt[3]{9}\n=3^{3+1/2+2/3}\n=3^{25/6}.\n\\]\nTherefore its base-3 logarithm is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{25}{6}=4\\frac16}\\), choice B.",
